diff --git a/docs/docker-deployment.md b/docs/docker-deployment.md
index f6eca78..ad4047e 100644
--- a/docs/docker-deployment.md
+++ b/docs/docker-deployment.md
@@ -101,6 +101,24 @@ Set `BASE_URL` to the full URL where your Fizzy instance is accessible:
 docker run --env BASE_URL=https://fizzy.example.com ...
 ```
 
+#### Push notifications (optional)
+
+Fizzy can send browser push notifications to phones and desktops: whatever lands in someone's notification tray also shows up on the devices where they've turned push notifications on (from their notification settings).
+
+Push notifications are signed with a VAPID key pair. Generate one with:
+
+```sh
+docker run --rm fizzy bin/rails runner 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{key.public_key}", "VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{key.private_key}"'
+```
+
+Then set both keys:
+
+- `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` - the public key, which browsers use to subscribe to push notifications
+- `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` - the private key, used to sign each push. Keep this secret.
+- `VAPID_SUBJECT` (optional) - a `mailto:` or `https:` contact for push services. Defaults to `mailto:` with `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS`.
+
+Push notifications stay off until both keys are set. Keep the same key pair across deploys: changing it means everyone has to turn push notifications on again.
+
 #### S3 storage (optional)
 
 If you'd prefer that uploaded files were stored in an S3 bucket rather than in your mounted volume, you can set that up.
